      "sketch": "Replace the explicit accessor methods with Python properties or convert the class to a `@dataclass`. This removes the four separate methods from the method-attribute graph, leaving only `__init__` and `is_premium`. Since `__init__` touches all attributes, it connects them, and `is_premium` touches `tier`, the graph becomes connected, reducing LCOM4 to 1. NOM will drop from 5 to 1 (only `is_premium` remains as a non-dunder method)."
