  "risk_notes": "Converting to a dataclass or using properties changes the public API from method calls (e.g., `customer.name()`) to attribute access (e.g., `customer.name`). This requires updating all call sites in the codebase. However, since this is a domain entity, the change is generally safe and improves idiomatic Python design. The LCOM4 metric is known to penalize data classes, so this refactoring aligns the code with the metric's intent by removing the artificial separation of accessors."
